## Why This Is Asked
Tests bridging basics, event streams, and hooks with real device APIs, plus practical UI wiring. It introduces platform quirks (Android vs iOS battery APIs) and emphasizes energy impact.

## Key Concepts
- Native modules and TurboModules/JSI bridging
- NativeEventEmitter and React hooks for streaming data
- Platform-specific battery APIs and background threading
- Lightweight UI binding to live data
- Privacy and energy considerations (polling interval, Doze modes)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: useBatteryStream hook (JS side)
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import { NativeEventEmitter, NativeModules } from 'react-native';
const { BatteryWatcher } = NativeModules;
const emitter = new NativeEventEmitter(BatteryWatcher);

export function useBatteryStream() {
  const [state, setState] = useState({ level: -1, ts: 0, belowThreshold: false });
  useEffect(() => {
    const sub = emitter.addListener('BatteryUpdate', (payload) => {
      setState(payload);
    });
    return () => sub.remove();
  }, []);
  return state;
}
```

